  "body": "## Cause\n\nAfter #2760 the fig8 mesh is finer. The 2D Adaptive Outside region of the biggest fig8 patch has a hole whose rightmost vertex looks onto a steep, short outer edge. `merge_hole` in `Region::triangles` bridged the hole to the computed ray hit on that edge. The hit point rounds to a point 3e-16 inside the material. The ear clipper then reads it as strictly inside the ears beside it and stops with \"no ear in a non-triangle walk\". Thus `boundary_viz::preview_fill` gave `None`, and the four frame-cost tests failed. The product code was wrong, not the test helper.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `crates/geometry/src/geo2d.rs` (`merge_hole`): the bridge candidates are now the walk vertices first, nearest first. The computed ray hits are the last resort. The same checks (no proper crossing, on material) accept or refuse each bridge. A bridge to an existing vertex adds no new point.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/geo2d.rs`: new pin `region_triangles_bridge_a_hole_to_a_steep_edge`. `check_triangles` gets an offset form, `check_triangles_in`.\n- `docs/decisions/2762-hole-bridge-vertex-first.md`: the decision entry.\n\n#2760 is not reverted. No gouge or containment check changed.\n\n## Readings\n\n- fig8 Outside region: before the fix, no triangulation. After the fix, 1990 triangles. Their area is 6225.768562612561 and the region area is 6225.76856261258.\n- The None and Inside regions keep their area.\n- The new geometry test fails on the old code: the fill area is 1814.03 against 2223.39, with no error. That is a silent loss of area.\n\n## Pinning tests (green on this code before the gate)\n\n- `frame_cost_caches::pick_lines_build_once_per_input`\n- `frame_cost_caches::pick_chips_group_the_welded_faces_once_and_follow_the_picks`\n- `frame_cost_probe::area_preview_fill_is_made_once_per_draft`\n- `frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`\n- The other frame_cost UI tests (8 in total) are green.\n- `region_triangles_bridge_a_hole_to_a_steep_edge` and the geometry `geo2d` suite are green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nThe code commit is b679bbe56. Head 1902ca054 changes only the decision file.\n\n## Effect on toolpaths\n\n`Region::triangles` is not display-only. `motion::entry::dive_room` takes the centroid of the largest clear triangle as the plunge or helix point. A region with a hole can thus get a different dive point. Each candidate is still checked with `Region::contains` and `boundary_clears`, so a changed point stays inside the room.\n\nHow I checked: `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --lib --test machining2d --test adaptive_hsm --test lead_room` is green on this head (451 + 2 + 4 + 68 passed, 0 failed).\n\n## Gate\n\nThe quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) falls back to batch because geometry changed. It is still in progress: 222 steps done, 0 failures, at step 223 of about 900. A PR comment will give the final numbers.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app golden CL and G-code suites (for example `golden_cl`, `regression_models`, `first_part_programs`) are not yet run. They are in the batch plan. If a golden output changes because of a new dive point, the gate shows it.\n- The heavy release lanes and the pixel snapshots are not run.\n- `geo2d.rs` was over 400 lines before this change (now 766). The split is not part of this fix.\n\nChangelog: fix: the 2D area preview fill and the dive-point triangulation no longer fail or lose area when a hole bridges to a steep, short boundary edge.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #2762\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
